    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0133" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">648T.006/21: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-09">April 9,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received April 9—11:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>883. Your 1638, December 19, 7 p.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d104-f1"/> and your
                    mail instruction 1134, December 26<anchor n="66" xml:id="d104-f2"/> regarding
                    exchange control and import license system in Palestine, other British Mandates
                    and British Territories within the Congo Basin. A lengthy note today received
                    from Foreign Office<anchor n="68" xml:id="d104-f3"/> is being forwarded by pouch
                    leaving April 11.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
